@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed private cache reuse behind current eligibility
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Caller
participant "Resource / retrieval owner" as H
participant "Current authority and revision state" as A
participant "Private cache / artifact lookup" as C
participant "Protected serving / storage" as F
Caller -> H : exact resource / variant / language context
H -> A : current eligibility + allowed revision / mode / scope
A --> H : current versioned context or denial
alt permitted context
 H -> C : exact scoped immutable input identity
 C --> H : matching usable identity or cache miss
 opt safe authorized cache miss
  H -> H : resolve / build through owning contract
 end
 H -> H : guarded delivery admission against current context
 H -> F : exact permitted artifact + controlled delivery scope
 F --> Caller : permitted bytes or accurate unavailable state
else denied / unresolved authority
 H --> Caller : safe denial; no stale positive fallback
end
note over H,F
 A cache hit is not authorization or proof of usable matching bytes.
 Invalidation/refill races require version validation or evaluated synchronization.
 Already emitted bytes cannot be recalled; later requests need current checks.
end note
@enduml
